From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OKO build <oko@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] build: fall back to /dev/urandom when sys/random.h is unusable

The vendor uclibc-ng 1.0.31 toolchain ships a sys/random.h that does not
compile on its own: the getrandom() prototype uses size_t without pulling
in <stddef.h>, and GRND_NONBLOCK is only defined for _GNU_SOURCE builds.
Meson reports the header as missing (cc.check_header) but still detects
the libc symbol (cc.has_function), so DBus is built with HAVE_GETRANDOM
and without HAVE_SYS_RANDOM_H:

  dbus-sysdeps-unix.c: error: 'GRND_NONBLOCK' undeclared
  warning: implicit declaration of function 'getrandom'

Disable HAVE_GETRANDOM whenever the header check fails.  DBus then uses
its portable /dev/urandom fallback, which is what the feature is for.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -736,6 +736,14 @@
     config.set(macro, cc.check_header(header, args: compile_args_c) ? 1 : false)
 endforeach
 
+# uclibc-ng ships a sys/random.h that does not compile standalone (it uses
+# size_t without including <stddef.h>), so check_header() fails while
+# has_function('getrandom') still succeeds.  Building the call without a
+# prototype and without GRND_* fails, so fall back to the /dev/urandom path.
+if not cc.check_header('sys/random.h', args: compile_args_c)
+    config.set('HAVE_GETRANDOM', false)
+endif
+
 execinfo = cc.find_library('execinfo', required: false)
 have_backtrace = (cc.has_header('execinfo.h', args: compile_args_c)
     and cc.has_function('backtrace', dependencies: execinfo, args: compile_args_c)
-- 
2.39.5
